76
00:06:19.056 --> 00:06:25.985
NARRATOR: On screen, create a rubric with
criteria: 'Cluster Alignment', 'Feasibility',

77
00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:31.024
'Learning Outcomes', and 'Resource
Availability', with scoring scales.

78
00:06:31.024 --> 00:06:37.201
NARRATOR: Change one assumption at a time and
observe which part of the reasoning no longer

79
00:06:37.201 --> 00:06:37.587
holds.

80
00:06:37.587 --> 00:06:43.917
NARRATOR: The edge case reveals the boundary
of the claim without discarding the useful

81
00:06:43.917 --> 00:06:44.821
core idea.

82
00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:51.803
NARRATOR: Use Representative Examples of
Theory Courses to diagnose a failure by

83
00:06:51.803 --> 00:06:55.239
separating symptoms, causes, and corrective
action.

84
00:06:55.239 --> 00:07:03.091
NARRATOR: OpenDSA presents data structures and
algorithms through executable visualizations

85
00:07:03.091 --> 00:07:04.661
